WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.250
Weeks after he announced his return as Superman,
Henry Cavill is out of a job – but at least

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:07.600
he seems to have gotten a hefty severance
package.

00:00:08.116 --> 00:00:10.260
"Well that was fun, while it didn't last."

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:15.059
As the DC Extended Universe prepared to kick
off in 2013, fans learned that Henry Cavill

00:00:15.059 --> 00:00:16.950
would be the next actor to portray Superman.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:22.019
He made his debut via director Zack Snyder's
"Man of Steel," and for a few years, he continued

00:00:22.019 --> 00:00:24.609
to feature prominently in the new cinematic
franchise.

00:00:24.609 --> 00:00:28.970
However, in the wake of the disastrous 2017
release of "Justice League," he basically

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:33.390
disappeared from the DCEU spotlight, leading
many folks to wonder if they'd ever see him

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:37.050
don the cape consistently again or if Warner
Bros. wanted to take "The Man of Tomorrow"

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:38.170
in a new direction.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:43.245
As speculation ran rampant, out of the blue,
Cavill got the chance to play Superman once more.

00:00:43.245 --> 00:00:48.210
In 2022's "Black Adam," he appeared in an
additional scene to confront Teth-Adam himself,

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:52.521
seemingly promising a Black Adam-Superman
showdown sometime in the future.

00:00:52.521 --> 00:00:54.700
Sadly, as we now know, this isn't going to
happen.

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:59.620
As the DC shared universe enters a reset period,
Cavill has been removed from the role of Superman

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:00.620
going forward.

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:04.670
This is arguably the best move for DC Studios
at this point, but it's just too bad his time

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:07.592
as Kal-El came to an end so unceremoniously.

00:01:07.592 --> 00:01:09.537
"Oh see now that's cold, that's a betrayal.

00:01:10.328 --> 00:01:11.330
I feel stung by that."

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:13.930
At the same time, one can't feel too bad for
Henry Cavill.

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:18.909
After all, he allegedly landed quite a hefty
payday for his brief "Black Adam" cameo.

00:01:18.909 --> 00:01:22.060
"I have a second chance, Lo.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:25.740
And I am not gonna waste it."

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:30.010
According to Umberto Gonzalez of The Wrap
on Twitter, Henry Cavill's incredibly short

00:01:30.010 --> 00:01:33.970
Superman scene in "Black Adam" reportedly
lined his pockets quite nicely.

00:01:33.970 --> 00:01:39.090
Gonzalez claims that Cavill scored around
$250,000 for his quick cameo, but that pales

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:43.579
in comparison to his payout as Geralt of Rivia
— a lead role he's also recently lost — for

00:01:43.579 --> 00:01:44.640
Netflix's "The Witcher."

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:50.000
Cosmopolitan notes that for the first season,
he was paid roughly $400,000 per episode,

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.990
which was upped to over $1 million per episode
for Season 2.

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:57.140
Of course, one has to remember that these
numbers were for full episodes, not a scene

00:01:57.140 --> 00:01:58.970
that clocked in under a minute.

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:04.049
Additionally, Gonzalez reveals that Cavill
was also paid for one other cameo in a yet-unreleased

00:02:04.049 --> 00:02:05.649
DC Comics-based production.

00:02:05.649 --> 00:02:09.960
The controversy-ridden "Flash" from director
Andy Muschietti supposedly included a cameo

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:11.930
by Cavill as Superman as well.

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:16.940
This is said to have netted him an additional
$250,000, bringing his recent DC pay up to

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:19.470
a staggering $500,000 in total.

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:23.660
However, unlike the "Black Adam" guest spot,
we more than likely won't get to see Cavill's

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:25.070
"Flash" appearance.

00:02:25.070 --> 00:02:28.690
Reports indicate that the scene involving
him wound up on the cutting room floor, likely

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:30.381
due to his Superman departure.

00:02:30.381 --> 00:02:33.115
"Well, I knew you didn't bring me back because
you liked me."

00:02:33.115 --> 00:02:37.269
Based on these numbers, it's hard to dispute
that Superman has been an incredible moneymaker

00:02:37.269 --> 00:02:39.050
for Henry Cavill over the years.

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:43.030
At the same time, one has to question if it
was ever truly about the money for him.

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:47.190
It's impossible to deny how much he adores
the character, as evidenced by his performances

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:49.420
and the way he's talked about it over the
past decade.

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:53.250
If you really want hard-hitting proof of his
love for Superman, though, look no further

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:57.090
than the Instagram post he made to announce
that his time as "The Man of Steel" had officially

00:02:57.090 --> 00:02:58.090
come to an end.

00:02:58.090 --> 00:02:59.850
In his emotional post, he wrote,

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:16.069
Time will tell who will be fortunate enough
to play Superman next, but they clearly have

00:03:16.069 --> 00:03:17.019
some big shoes to fill.

